      "question": "The curve C has equation y = 27x^(1/2) - x^(3/2) - 20, x > 0. Find dy/dx, giving each term in simplest form.",
      "status": "ready",
      "answer": "dy/dx = (27/2)x^(-1/2) - (3/2)x^(1/2)",
      "steps": [
        "Write each term as a power of x: 27x^(1/2), -x^(3/2), -20.",
        "Use the power rule: d/dx of x^n is n x^(n-1).",
        "27x^(1/2) gives 27 x (1/2) x^(-1/2) = (27/2)x^(-1/2).",
        "-x^(3/2) gives -(3/2)x^(1/2).",
        "The constant -20 differentiates to 0.",
        "So dy/dx = (27/2)x^(-1/2) - (3/2)x^(1/2)."
      ]
    },
