      "question": "Find d^2y/dx^2 and hence determine the nature of the stationary point of C at x = 9.",
      "status": "ready",
      "answer": "d^2y/dx^2 = -(27/4)x^(-3/2) - (3/4)x^(-1/2); at x = 9 this is -1/2 < 0, so the point is a maximum.",
      "steps": [
        "Differentiate dy/dx = (27/2)x^(-1/2) - (3/2)x^(1/2) term by term.",
        "(27/2)(-1/2)x^(-3/2) = -(27/4)x^(-3/2), and -(3/2)(1/2)x^(-1/2) = -(3/4)x^(-1/2).",
