      "question": "The annual profit P (thousands of pounds) from watches sold at selling price GBP x is modelled by P = 12x - x^(3/2) - 120. Using calculus, find the maximum possible annual profit.",
      "status": "ready",
      "answer": "Maximum annual profit is 136 thousand pounds (GBP 136 000), reached at x = 64.",
      "steps": [
        "Differentiate: dP/dx = 12 - (3/2)x^(1/2).",
        "Set dP/dx = 0: (3/2)x^(1/2) = 12, so x^(1/2) = 8.",
        "Square both sides: x = 64.",
        "Substitute: P = 12(64) - 64^(3/2) - 120.",
        "64^(3/2) = 8^3 = 512, so P = 768 - 512 - 120 = 136.",
        "The maximum profit is 136 thousand pounds."
      ]
    },
