      "question": "A curve C has equation y = 4x^3 - 9x + k/x, x > 0, where k is a constant. The point P with x coordinate 1/2 lies on C and is a stationary point of C. Show that k = -3/2.",
      "status": "ready",
      "answer": "k = -3/2 (shown)",
      "steps": [
        "Write y = 4x^3 - 9x + kx^(-1).",
        "Differentiate: dy/dx = 12x^2 - 9 - kx^(-2).",
        "At P, x = 1/2 and dy/dx = 0: 12(1/4) - 9 - 4k = 0.",
        "So 3 - 9 - 4k = 0, which gives -6 - 4k = 0.",
        "Solving gives k = -3/2."
      ]
