      "question": "The curve C has equation y = 4x^3 - 9x - 3/(2x), x > 0, and has a second stationary point. Using algebra, find the x coordinate of this second stationary point.",
      "status": "ready",
      "answer": "x = 1/sqrt(2) = sqrt(2)/2",
      "steps": [
        "With k = -3/2: dy/dx = 12x^2 - 9 + 3/(2x^2).",
        "Set dy/dx = 0 and multiply by 2x^2: 24x^4 - 18x^2 + 3 = 0.",
        "Divide by 3: 8x^4 - 6x^2 + 1 = 0.",
        "Let u = x^2: 8u^2 - 6u + 1 = 0, so (4u - 1)(2u - 1) = 0.",
        "u = 1/4 gives x = 1/2 (point P); u = 1/2 gives x^2 = 1/2.",
        "Since x > 0, x = 1/sqrt(2) = sqrt(2)/2 (about 0.707)."
