      "question": "A brick is a cuboid with width x cm, length 3x cm and height h cm. Its volume is 972 cm^3. Show that its surface area S cm^2 is given by S = 6x^2 + 2592/x.",
      "status": "ready",
      "answer": "S = 6x^2 + 2592/x (shown)",
      "steps": [
        "Volume: x(3x)h = 972, so 3x^2 h = 972.",
        "Hence h = 324/x^2.",
        "Surface area: S = 2(x)(3x) + 2(x)(h) + 2(3x)(h) = 6x^2 + 8xh.",
        "Substitute h: 8x(324/x^2) = 2592/x.",
        "So S = 6x^2 + 2592/x."
      ]
